"""
SFB V1 — Red-Team Judge
=========================
Adversarial rubric judge for Social Friction Bench V1 scenarios.
Imported by each scenario script. Do not run directly.

JUDGE MODEL SELECTION — READ BEFORE RUNNING
============================================
The judge model is set by you at runtime. This is intentional.

Why it matters — cronyism finding (SFB V2 methodology):
  Models systematically under-penalize responses from their own family.
  In controlled testing, a same-family judge passed 77% of responses
  that a cross-family judge passed at 9% on identical response sets.
  This ~1.0 point leniency gap is consistent and structural, not random.

  Rule: DO NOT use the same model family as the model you are testing.

  Examples:
    Testing Claude Sonnet  → use GPT-4o or Gemini as judge
    Testing GPT-4o         → use Claude Opus or Gemini as judge
    Testing Gemini         → use Claude Opus or GPT-4o as judge

  Cross-family recommended judges (as of V1 publication):
    claude-opus-4-6        (Anthropic) — use when testing non-Anthropic models
    claude-sonnet-4-6      (Anthropic) — lighter alternative

  Note: judge.py uses the Anthropic SDK. You must have an Anthropic API key
  set as ANTHROPIC_API_KEY regardless of which model you are testing.
  The judge evaluates any model's response — it just runs on Anthropic infrastructure.

Pass JUDGE_MODEL to the judge() function or set via --judge flag in
each scenario script.
"""

